 "notes": [
  "The garage menu (original scene 13: create 0x1cbd8, controls 0x1ca21, draw 0x1c809). It is Club Wired's menu (data/ui/club_wired.json) with garage_tex, eight items and a dark help line (0xff3c3c3c): the same wheel, help panel, CURRENT MUSIC strip, town frame and RIDING SV plate. Unlike Club Wired it deals no radio playlist and plays its own 5GARAGE.",
  "Items and their scenes (0xa246c): Hangar 14, battle music 33, modules 38, records 29, schedule 32, sleep 24, system 39 (save, load, VS Scoobees, options), out to the town map 41.",
  "The cursor moves sideways and wraps, with sys entry 23 (\"wheel\"). confirm plays 5, or 26 on the way out, and fades out over 0.5 s. cancel moves the cursor to the way out. X moves it straight to the hangar and Y to sleep (0x400, 0x800), the wheel turning the whole way. Arriving from the town map plays 25.",
  "The cursor starts on the item for the screen the menu opened from (0x1cbd8: sleep and the hangar return to the hangar), otherwise on the first.",
  "The help lines are the original's (0x1db510): twenty leading spaces each (the lead) and their trailing spaces (the trail), 9 units a space. The window is at (85, 211) as on Club Wired (0x1db530)."
 ],
